  "original_cues": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "start": 0.13,
      "end": 4.766,
      "text": "An AI tool can keep yesterday’s approval after the evidence changes. How does",
      "first_word": 0,
      "last_word": 12
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "start": 4.796,
      "end": 6.281,
      "text": "the next reader know?",
      "first_word": 13,
      "last_word": 16
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "start": 8.13,
      "end": 13.791,
      "text": "I built Arkiv Graph: a graph SDK over Arkiv’s public indexed entities. Signed",
      "first_word": 17,
      "last_word": 29
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "start": 13.821,
      "end": 18.168,
      "text": "manifests bind every graph member. Readers assemble and traverse the",
      "first_word": 30,
      "last_word": 39
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "start": 18.198,
      "end": 19.124,
      "text": "graph locally.",
      "first_word": 40,
      "last_word": 41
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "start": 20.13,
      "end": 24.745,
      "text": "AI Passport checks approval before inference. It links untrusted Qarinah",
      "first_word": 42,
      "last_word": 51
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "start": 24.775,
      "end": 30.399,
      "text": "context to source bytes. Try coding guards, rupee tools, and UPI safety.",
      "first_word": 52,
      "last_word": 63
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "start": 32.13,
      "end": 36.319,
      "text": "In the recorded testnet lifecycle, two project-operated readers first admitted",
      "first_word": 64,
      "last_word": 73
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "start": 36.349,
      "end": 40.96,
      "text": "the task. A real review withdrawal followed. Each reader’s next request",
      "first_word": 74,
      "last_word": 84
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "start": 40.99,
      "end": 43.572,
      "text": "refused it. These guards are deterministic.",
      "first_word": 85,
      "last_word": 90
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "start": 44.13,
      "end": 49.351,
      "text": "Root updates now follow a pinned authority and scope. Signed revisions link",
      "first_word": 91,
      "last_word": 102
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "start": 49.381,
      "end": 54.165,
      "text": "the previous digest and root. A retained checkpoint rejects observed rollback.",
      "first_word": 103,
      "last_word": 113
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "start": 54.195,
      "end": 58.978,
      "text": "Two revisions and their tiny graphs were published together, in one",
      "first_word": 114,
      "last_word": 124
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "start": 59.008,
      "end": 62.121,
      "text": "transaction. The larger AI graph remains pinned.",
      "first_word": 125,
      "last_word": 131
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "start": 64.13,
      "end": 69.069,
      "text": "The live reader verifies both signed revisions at one explicit snapshot, then",
      "first_word": 132,
      "last_word": 143
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "start": 69.099,
      "end": 71.22,
      "text": "reconstructs the complete current graph.",
      "first_word": 144,
      "last_word": 148
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "start": 72.13,
      "end": 76.654,
      "text": "Controlled replays hide the newer head or edit signed root bytes. Both are",
      "first_word": 149,
      "last_word": 161
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "start": 76.684,
      "end": 78.836,
      "text": "refused. This is a local test.",
      "first_word": 162,
      "last_word": 167
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "start": 80.13,
      "end": 85.669,
      "text": "A signed withdrawal can arrive before its target. The journal retains it, then",
      "first_word": 168,
      "last_word": 180
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "start": 85.699,
      "end": 90.809,
      "text": "checks it when the review reappears. State must persist before admission. A",
      "first_word": 181,
      "last_word": 192
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "start": 90.839,
      "end": 95.092,
      "text": "shared browser lock serializes tab updates. Deleting local history still",
      "first_word": 193,
      "last_word": 202
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "start": 95.122,
      "end": 96.457,
      "text": "removes this protection.",
      "first_word": 203,
      "last_word": 205
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "start": 98.13,
      "end": 103.802,
      "text": "Here the deployed app reads the public session again and refuses a new task.",
      "first_word": 206,
      "last_word": 219
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "start": 103.832,
      "end": 108.282,
      "text": "The historical acceptance stays visible as history. Both clients and signing",
      "first_word": 220,
      "last_word": 230
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "start": 108.312,
      "end": 111.645,
      "text": "wallets are project-controlled; external adoption is not claimed.",
      "first_word": 231,
      "last_word": 238
    },
    {
      "id": 26,
      "start": 112.13,
      "end": 117.314,
      "text": "Repeated checks must stay usable on mobile. Eighteen simulated audits: three",
      "first_word": 239,
      "last_word": 249
    },
    {
      "id": 27,
      "start": 117.344,
      "end": 122.054,
      "text": "cold loads per route and phase. Median scores reached ninety-eight,",
      "first_word": 250,
      "last_word": 259
    },
    {
      "id": 28,
      "start": 122.084,
      "end": 126.32,
      "text": "ninety-eight, and ninety-six. Desktop lab results, not physical-phone or",
      "first_word": 260,
      "last_word": 268
    },
    {
      "id": 29,
      "start": 126.35,
      "end": 127.348,
      "text": "field data.",
      "first_word": 269,
      "last_word": 270
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "start": 128.13,
      "end": 133.644,
      "text": "A hash identifies bytes. A private database depends on its operator. Arkiv",
      "first_word": 271,
      "last_word": 282
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "start": 133.674,
      "end": 139.187,
      "text": "provides shared indexed discovery. Readers can bypass our API. The SDK adds",
      "first_word": 283,
      "last_word": 294
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "start": 139.217,
      "end": 141.577,
      "text": "graph verification and AI context.",
      "first_word": 295,
      "last_word": 299
    },
    {
      "id": 33,
      "start": 142.13,
      "end": 147.513,
      "text": "Install Arkiv Graph zero point four, or AI Passport zero point six. Public",
      "first_word": 300,
      "last_word": 312
    },
    {
      "id": 34,
      "start": 147.543,
      "end": 152.094,
      "text": "schemas, queries and evidence make the demo reproducible. Outside usage is",
      "first_word": 313,
      "last_word": 323
    },
    {
      "id": 35,
      "start": 152.124,
      "end": 153.423,
      "text": "not yet proven.",
      "first_word": 324,
      "last_word": 326
    },
    {
      "id": 36,
      "start": 154.13,
      "end": 158.953,
      "text": "One RPC remains trusted. Unseen omissions remain possible. Build your",
      "first_word": 327,
      "last_word": 336
    },
    {
      "id": 37,
      "start": 158.983,
      "end": 160.004,
      "text": "own reader.",
      "first_word": 337,
      "last_word": 338
    }
  ],
